1. WHAT THIS REPOSITORY IS

This repository is an index to InferenceInterviews.com (https://inferenceinterviews.com). It lists a
selection of interview question prompts, topic names, concept names, course
and guide titles, and screenshots of the site, each linking to the original
page. The selection, arrangement, wording and screenshots are original works
protected by copyright, both individually and as a compilation.

The worked answers, concept explanations, courses, guides, tools and every
other part of InferenceInterviews.com are not included here. They are governed by the
site's own terms at https://inferenceinterviews.com.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

  (a) Read this repository on GitHub and follow its links.
  (b) Use it for your own personal, non-commercial interview preparation,
      including keeping a private copy for that purpose only.
  (c) Link to this repository or to any page of InferenceInterviews.com.
  (d) Fork it on GitHub, only to the extent GitHub's Terms of Service grant
      that right to other GitHub users. A fork remains subject to this
      licence, and forking waives none of the restrictions in section 3.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT OUR WRITTEN PERMISSION

  (a) Republish, mirror or redistribute any part of this repository, in
      original or modified form, on any website, app, course, book, PDF,
      newsletter, social media post, question bank or other product.
  (b) Scrape, crawl, bulk-download or extract the contents by automated
      means, other than ordinary search-engine indexing that links back to
      the original.
  (c) Use any part of the contents to train, fine-tune, evaluate, benchmark,
      ground or prompt a machine learning model or AI system, or include it
      in a dataset, embedding index, vector store or retrieval corpus.
  (d) Direct, permit or rely on an AI agent, assistant or automated tool to
      do any of the things listed in (a) to (c).
  (e) Rewrite, paraphrase, translate, reorder or recombine the questions to
      produce a substitute question bank or study product.
  (f) Remove or alter this notice, the attribution links, or the identifiers
      embedded in the files.

4. ENFORCEMENT

The files in this repository carry identifiers that let us trace copies.
Where we find material copied from this repository or from InferenceInterviews.com, we
will send takedown notices to the hosting provider, search engines,
marketplaces and app stores concerned, including notices under the United
States Digital Millennium Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. section 512) and under
the Indian Copyright Act, 1957 and the Information Technology (Intermediary
Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021. We reserve all other
rights and remedies, including claims for damages.

